From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Weegee <748975+Weegee@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:54:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] drv: split probe into setup and hardware bring-up, add
 power-cycle recovery

Probe and remove did everything in one sequence, so the only way to
restart the camera was unloading the driver. Separate the one-time PCI
and V4L2 setup from bringing the S2 chip and ISP firmware up and down,
and track the hardware state.

fthd_hw_restart() tears the chip down, optionally cuts its power through
the ACPI CMPE method (off 250 ms, on 20 ms, as the macOS driver does),
restores the PCI config space, brings the firmware up again and resumes
a running stream. A work item runs it up to three times; on final
failure all buffers are returned with an error.

V4L2 buffers now survive a restart: their S2 descriptors and IOMMU
entries are released on teardown and recreated on bring-up, and buffers
the firmware held are sent again. Firmware supplied buffer tags are
checked before use. Controls share the queue lock so they cannot race
a restart.

Also fixes:
- double free of the IOMMU allocator on a repeated teardown
- probe failure leaking the BAR mappings
- irq_work freeing the interrupt it runs from when the IRQ is stuck;
  it now only closes the interrupt gate
- debugfs channel files dereferencing freed channels

debugfs gains "state" and "recover" (write: power cycle and wait).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
